# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**When a long-running command streams its output to a `/tmp/<name>.log` file** (e.g. background `make compose-deploy`, `make act-*`, or any `… 2>&1 | tee /tmp/<name>.log`), you MUST tell the operator the concrete `tail -f /tmp/<name>.log` command they can run in another terminal to follow the log live. Include the full path literally so it is copy-pasteable."
